Hello RGRN,

This is my first patch for Nethack. It introduces a new counter
(displayed as a #conduct), which tries to measure the total amount of
pain the inhabitants of the dungeon suffered through the game.

One may pursue the goal of bringing the least amount of pain or mental
suffering to the monsters:). This means that you try to make sure nobody
gets hurt, and if a monster has to die, you kill it with one or two
blows, and don't stab him thirty times with your thoroughly rusty knife;
the more the monster is wounded, the more it suffers. However, an
anaesthesized (sleeping/paralyzed) patient doesn't suffer, and you can
stab it all the way you like. Scared, trapped, blinded, cancelled
monsters suffer mentally; it is your duty to deliver them a coup de
grace to relieve them from their sufferings:) Engraving with wands of
fire, lightning and magic missile may hurt the bugs on the floor, and
their suffering will add to the total (so perma-Elbereths are a bit
penalized). You might also want to untrap all the traps you find, so
that an unwary dungeon dweller would not get hit by a boulder and suffer
unduly. Instakills become more valuable. Genocide counts as many instant
kills. Healing your pets becomes more valuable, as their sufferings add
up too. +oSleep becomes even more valuable. Best pets probably include
purple worms (instakill) and guardian nagas (anaesthesy). At the moment,
all kills add 1 to total suffering; whether or not a monster killed in
its sleep suffers is a delicate question (if it doesn't, sleeping gas
traps become real useful).

Another goal, of course, is to deliver the most pain per kill, where
everything gets just the opposite:)

The patch is available as

http://doublef.nm.ru/violence.patch

(it's against unpatched 3.4.3). It breaks saves, but (hopefully) not
bones.

Any comments, especially corrections to the suffering weights and the
wording of messages, are appreciated.

